+## The idea in one minute
 
-How the parts talk to each other is defined in [INTEGRATION.md](INTEGRATION.md). Design rules are in [DESIGN.md](DESIGN.md), the system in [ARCHITECTURE.md](ARCHITECTURE.md), the demo in [DEMO.md](DEMO.md), status in [PROGRESS.md](PROGRESS.md) and reasoning in [DECISIONS.md](DECISIONS.md).
+**The problem.** Moving to Abu Dhabi is not one task. It is a chain of dependent steps spread across parties that do not share a record: the employer, the immigration and ID services, a landlord, a bank, an insurer. The Emirates ID application needs the visa. The bank account needs the Emirates ID application. Family sponsorship needs a registered tenancy. Each step produces the documents the next one needs, so a missing document or a silent delay at one party stalls everything after it, and nobody can see why. The newcomer waits without knowing what for. The employer cannot tell where a hire is stuck. And along the way people hand passports and salary details to strangers.
 
-## Requirements
+**The idea.** Give everyone in the chain the same live record, and put an agent in the middle that does the legwork. Three principles make it different from a checklist:
 
-- Node 22 or later
-- npm 10 or later
+1. **A roadmap that understands dependencies.** Steps unlock when their prerequisites are done, and every step explains in plain language why it is there. A hire's stage and status are derived from the steps, so the dashboards cannot drift from reality.
+2. **The agent proposes, the person decides.** The agent reads documents, drafts applications and asks. Nothing is sent until the newcomer approves, and the approval card shows who receives it, what is attached and what is deliberately left out.
+3. **Privacy decided by policy, not by the agent.** Every piece of personal data carries a label (passport, salary, health and so on). A policy sidecar, [Rasikh Guard](packages/rasikh-guard), decides for each label and each destination whether it may leave: allowed, needs the person's consent, only as a derived result, or never. A landlord gets "affordability: yes", never the salary.
 
-## Install and run
+**Why Abu Dhabi.** The steps, services and vocabulary are local: TAMM, UAE PASS, Emirates ID, Tawtheeq tenancy registration, Abu Dhabi neighbourhoods, AED, English and Arabic with full right-to-left support. A second module helps a foreign company open an Abu Dhabi branch and then moves its first employees into the same relocation pipeline.
+
